{"baseRefName":"main","baseRefOid":"4661a24b599d75503a997f3ce122f3ad2da77048","body":"Scope input now has immutable domain references, configurable admission labels, live Linear membership reads, and an optional scope on the existing workflow request. Both `/workflow` and `/fire` validate the request into domain values before enqueueing; the queue carries the scope to execution. Existing unscoped requests retain their behavior and repository selection still requires exactly one source. Invalid fallback bases now return 422 before enqueue, while recorded bases retain precedence.\n\nLinear scope reads exhaust pagination, hydrate issue details, preserve structural relations, and reject observed membership changes between listing and detail reads. Initiative traversal detects cycles through child links while accepting shared-child DAGs; inconsistent detail identities raise typed errors. Instating configured scope labels creates missing native definitions without applying labels to entities.\n\nThis remains a draft. Scoped jobs resolve their input at execution time and explicitly report `ScopedExecutionUnavailableError` because the scope graph and tracker meta-label entry are not implemented. They never fall back to the unscoped pipeline. Measured milestone metadata omits its URL, so that metadata read refuses rather than inventing one. Reads are not transactional snapshots, and new connected-app tool contracts remain unverified with the deployment's service credential.\n\nValidation: `make check` passed at `5514b8d959a694f9985f27980a40ef1dd1779400`: formatting, Ruff, mypy, and 3,214 tests passed; 16 existing live-service/PostgreSQL tests skipped. Independent review verified request conversion, scope propagation, legacy behavior and eight valid behavior mutations. It caught and closed the empty-base validation regression and configured-tracker wiring coverage gap. The earlier scope/configuration/mapping mutation evidence remains recorded on the relevant Linear criteria. 